From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: area budget, AreaEvict spares returns and deletes about what a burst brought in (EDEN_UP_AREA_BUDGET)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (no upstream port): a pause menu's image burst made AreaEvict
(EDEN_NX2_AREA_EVICT) delete the whole field, rebuilt on close. Gated by EDEN_UP_AREA_BUDGET
(exact 1), a live switch (common/live_switch.h, Id AreaBudget, not armed); off by default. Does
nothing without EDEN_NX2_AREA_EVICT (boot). On: a burst made mostly of images AreaEvict deleted
within 600 frames opens no window; an opened window deletes about the fresh bytes of its burst
(oldest first, same candidates), never more than the old pass. A refusal or over-budget image
in the window gives the old unbudgeted window. EDEN_UP_AREA_BUDGET_VERIFY=1 (boot) keeps the old
deletions and counts what the new rule would have spared. 10 s line: "EDEN_AREA_BUDGET 10s:".

Reviewed draft from the memory job, v2: reviewer gave a refusal-opened window no budget (the old
window) and dropped the budget on a refusal or MemoryPressureEvents in an open window (new
"refusal fallbacks" counter), counted budget-capped passes even with nothing deleted, moved the
JoinImages byte count inside the switch, cast the ring position to u32, and made the verify
shadow follow the refusal rule.
